<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valsgärde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valsgärde is an archaeological burial site on the Fyris river north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Its boat graves, used for generations from about 600 to the 11th century, contained helmets, weapons, horses and feasting gear. Together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vendel">Vendel</a> they define the wealthy warrior culture of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Svear</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valsgarde.jpg" alt="Valsgärde" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Berig · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vallsg%C3%A4rde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
